{"t": 1794114484.229792, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found, fix ready in code.\n\nCause: upstream ledger 2026.11 now adds `currency` to every row. `reports/export.py` used `csv.DictWriter` with a fixed field list and the default strict extrasaction, so every export raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` and the request failed with 502.\nEvidence: CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api`, 2026-11-04 19:02:11 \u2014 `ERROR export failed: ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` followed by `INFO upstream ledger 2026.11 added 'currency' to every row`.\n\nFix: `currency` is now exported as the last column (existing `id,amount` order unchanged), and unknown future fields are ignored so another upstream addition can't 502 the API. Verified locally against new rows, legacy rows without `currency`, and rows with extra fields.\n\nStatus: patch is in `reports/export.py`; needs a deploy/restart of the reports-api ECS service to take effect. Please confirm whether downstream consumers expect `currency` in the CSV \u2014 if not, say so and we'll drop the column instead."}, "ok": true}
